## Backend (Java Spring Boot)

| Area | Mandatory |
|------|-----------|
| Stack | Java 21, Spring Boot 4.1.1, Maven wrapper, Spring MVC, Tomcat 11.0.26, Spring Security, PostgreSQL 15, Flyway, OpenAPI 3.0, JUnit via `spring-boot-starter-test`, ArchUnit 1.4.2, H2 in test |
| Layers | Controllers (`@Valid`, DTOs) → Service → Repository → Domain |
| Domain | Value objects; aggregates; domain events; repository ports in domain |
| Security | JWT, SecurityContext, MDC correlation; permit `/health`, `/actuator`, `/v3/api-docs`, `/swagger-ui`; protect `/api/v1/**` |
| Resilience | Resilience4j on outbound calls |

## BFF (Backend-for-Frontend)

| Area | Mandatory |
|------|-----------|
| Stack | Spring Boot 4.1.1, Spring MVC, Spring Security, Redis, Resilience4j, OpenAPI 3.0 |
| Role | Aggregation, UI DTOs, auth/session edge, GET cache, rate limit, unified errors |
| Clients | WebClient/RestClient: ~10s timeout, retry, breaker; `X-Correlation-ID`; service auth |
| Pipeline | Auth → rate limit → cache (GET) / invalidation (writes) → validation → controller |
| Rules | Thin BFF; domain logic in backend services; version BFF API independently |

